{"qid":"Q321371","names":["Cimmerian Bosporus"],"title":"Cimmerian Bosporus","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Bosporan Kingdom was a Greco-Scythian state centred on the Cimmerian Bosporus (modern Strait of Kerch), founded by the Spartocid dynasty after Spartocus overthrew the Archaeanactidae in 438 BCE. Its rulers controlled the grain and fish export trade vital to Athens; Leucon I (r. 389–349 BCE) granted Athenian merchants special privileges and was honoured with Athenian citizenship. After Mithridates VI Eupator absorbed the kingdom into his Pontic realm and his defeat by Rome in 63 BCE, it became a Roman client state, briefly incorporated into Moesia under Nero before restoration. The kingdom issued coins continuously into the mid-fourth century CE; Gothic and Hunnic pressure from the 270s onward weakened it fatally, and the final coin series under Rhescuporis VI dates to around 341 CE.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. The kingdom's numismatic record is exceptionally detailed and the Spartocid dynasty well-documented in Greek inscriptions and literary sources; territorial extent is attested for the core Crimean and Taman holdings but more approximate for periods of maximum Pontic expansion.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Bosporan Kingdom","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bosporan_Kingdom"},{"label":"Britannica: Bosporan Kingdom","url":"https://www.britannica.com/topic/Bosporan-Kingdom"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Spartocids","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spartocids"}],"britannica":"place/Kingdom-of-the-Bosporus","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Bosporan Kingdom","rulers":[{"qid":null,"n